--- CRITERION 3: both fields render in headline AND as two new columns after
    "Lifetime Tax"; taxopt-th-tooltip headers; glossary entries; conventional
    formatting; correct semantics -- PASS
Not verified by reading alone. I rendered the real template through the real
renderer (scratch probe test, since removed) and parsed the output:

  HEADLINE: "SS 67, Fill 24% bracket, 67->72 - Ending: $900,000.00 real
             . peak marginal: 40% . Roth converted: $123,456.00 nominal"
  thead labels (non-MC), in order:
    ['Strategy','SS (P/S)','End Portfolio','Lifetime Tax','Peak Rate','Roth Conv',
     'Delta vs Baseline']
    -> Peak Rate and Roth Conv are immediately after Lifetime Tax, as required.
  tbody row0 cells:
    [strategy, '67', '$900,000.00', '$150,000.00', '40%', '$123,456.00',
     '+$50,000.00']
    -> rate and money render in the table body in the correct positions.
  glossary <dt>s: ['Strategy','SS (P/S)','End Portfolio','Lifetime Tax',
                   'Peak Rate','Roth Conv','Delta vs Baseline']

Headers use the partial: template lines 65-70 both call
{{template "taxopt-th-tooltip" (dict "Label" "Peak Rate"/"Roth Conv" ...)}}.
Formatting follows convention: `{{printf "%.0f" ...}}%` for the rate (lines 28, 99)
and `{{formatMoney ...}}` for dollars (lines 29, 100).
Semantics conveyed: line 66/167 state the rate is "measured, not looked up in a
bracket table" and "can push it above every statutory bracket ... Reporting only --
not part of the ranking metric"; line 69/169 state "actually converted ... nominal
(not inflation-adjusted) dollars ... Reflects what the engine realized, not what was
planned."
OBSERVATION (not a failure): the Roth Conv header tooltip reads "in today's nominal
(not inflation-adjusted) dollars", while everywhere else in this file "today's
dollars" denotes REAL. The parenthetical disambiguates, and the glossary entry
(line 169) drops "today's" and is clean, so the semantics are conveyed; flagging only
as a wording tension.

